<!-- BEGIN custom:introduction -->
# cargo-cicd

`cargo-cicd` is a local-first CI/CD executor for Rust workspaces. Building,
testing, and publishing happen on the operator's machine, with the operator's
token. CI stays credential-free: it consumes evidence files, not secrets.

The design premise: an unverifiable claim is not evidence. Every command emits
a receipt; every verdict is backed by a file on disk whose integrity can be
checked independently. A claim that cannot be replayed from recorded evidence
does not count — an LLM's assertion cannot satisfy a gate.
<!-- END custom:introduction -->

## Install

```sh
cargo install cargo-cicd
```

Requires Rust (stable). Optional external tools — `act`, `gh`, `cyclonedx`,
`cargo semver-checks`, `just` — are discovered on `PATH` at runtime; a missing
tool produces a typed Unavailable failure, never a silent pass.

## Quickstart

```sh
cargo build                                          # build the workspace
cargo cicd status show                               # workspace snapshot (read-only)
cargo cicd ci run --dry-run                          # preview CI workflows locally
cargo cicd ocel export                               # export the event log (OCEL 2.0)
cargo cicd receipt verify                            # verify blake3 receipt integrity
```

## Command surface

`cargo cicd` uses a noun-verb grammar: 24 nouns, 56 verbs
(asserted by `tests/status.rs`):

| Noun | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `certification` | Show certification policy state |
| `ci` | Run GitHub Actions workflows locally (`act`) or remotely (`gh`) |
| `claude-context` | Show Claude integration context |
| `deploy` | Schema and MCP projections of the CLI surface |
| `doctor` | Workspace, evidence, and diff diagnostics |
| `evidence` | Audit, list, reset the evidence corpus |
| `gate` | Repository release gate evaluation |
| `git` | Status, branch close, diff, stage, commit, fetch |
| `hooks` | Install/uninstall Claude Code hooks; pre-tool-use checks |
| `lsp` | Check LLM-contamination invariants of public docs |
| `ocel` | Replay and export the OCEL 2.0 event log |
| `pipeline` | Run, inspect, validate command pipelines |
| `publish` | Run, check, validate crates.io publication |
| `receipt` | Verify and audit blake3-chained receipts |
| `release-gate` | Evaluate measured release gates |
| `sbom` | Generate and show SBOM artifacts |
| `standing` | Refresh, verify, report standing receipts |
| `status` | Workspace status show and audit |
| `target` | Target-directory size profile and prune |
| `test` | Changed-test, full run, and bench execution |
| `trace` | Profile recorded traces |
| `trybuild` | Compile-fail fixture verification |
| `verify` | Repository verification court |
| `workspace` | Doctor, validate, sync, list workspace health |

